(Cyclic list structure is depth-bounded, not stack-overflowing - plan
 040 stage 1e1 acceptance 5. Self-append creates a cycle; printing it
 recurses to the depth limit (64), prints a "..." truncation marker,
 sets the error flag, and unwinds safely. The `on error` block observes
 the flag.)

a list called x is [].
append x to x.
print x.
on error print "E".